From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Atelier <atelier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:34:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Generate mips with the engine's linear-light box filter;
 encode BC7 faster

Mips were bicubic-resized in sRGB space, which darkens every level (measured on
Marvel Rivals character textures: -0.4 at mip 1 growing to -4.3 by mip 5). Each
level is now a 2x2 box average of the previous one, in linear light for sRGB
textures and with straight (non-premultiplied) alpha; this reproduces the game's
own mips with ~0 bias.

BC7 at BestQuality took ~25s per 1366x1366 level, making exports look hung. BC7
now uses texconv when UASSETTOOL_TEXCONV names it (24x faster end to end), with
every mip padded to whole 4x4 blocks first (texconv's GPU encoder mishandles
partial blocks); otherwise BCnEncoder's Balanced mode (2x faster, +0.1-0.2 RMS).
Encoding runs in parallel.
---
 src/UAssetTool/Texture/TextureInjector.cs | 165 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 153 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/UAssetTool/Texture/TextureInjector.cs b/src/UAssetTool/Texture/TextureInjector.cs
index 2a55f39..ce4524c 100644
